        long tmp = len;
        while (p < ep) {
            sp = p;
            r = asn1_parse2(bp, &p, tmp, ...);
            ...
            tmp -= p - sp;
        }
    }
}
```

After the constructed block, `p` has advanced to `ep` (or beyond). Then at the end:
```c
length -= len;
```
Wait, but `length` here is the outer length, and `len` is the constructed content length. So `length -= len` subtracts the content length. But `p` has already advanced by `len` (the content). And `length` was already decremented by `hl` (the header) earlier. So `length -= len` makes `length` = original - header - content. That's correct.

