But here's the thing: `ASN1_get_object`'s check is `plen > omax - header`, i.e., `plen + header > omax`. And `asn1_check_tlen`'s check is `plen + header > len` (where `len == omax`). These are the SAME check! So if `ASN1_get_object` doesn't set the error bit (i.e., `plen + header <= omax`), then `asn1_check_tlen`'s check also passes. No overflow.

So the `asn1_check_tlen` overflow is NOT reachable because `ASN1_get_object` already bounds `plen`.

